{"kind":"report","text":"Approved complete draft6 of notes/2026-10-19-record-and-event-identifiers.md at104ad1419f7aaa2446cd5ce9a864beea352a9f9f/treefae865ad5a532d4d3f4d00bed0ae984f271e57f7. Full note read; primary effective/exact/direct plannerpromise,1/1nativeartifactquery exhausted and assigned prepare. Only authored path is this note from basedba3e762; actual reviewed Main/origin nowa00eda3b, whose separate G5a source changes are upstream, not authored by this design. No remaining findings under the amended D6 conditions.\n\nAll D5 findings resolved. Genesis construction now uses contextual relative self references{scope,genesis:null} only in genesis-originated retained seeds/messages/effects, preserves their sent bytes, resolves full references from authenticated source/delivery context, separates nonce-specific child causes in artroom-input-1, and computes the genesis digest after its sends. The Directory creation witness is explicitly required. Independent small ASCII/integer canonical-JSON dependency model computes all three child seed identities before sealing the parent, computes the parent digest once, preserves raw sent seeds and resolves creator from the source fact. Different nonces change both parent genesis and every child's identity. This establishes computability of the proposed dependency construction, not implementation correctness or native admission.\n\nThe worked Git script now rehashes each raw commit, reads its raw first parent, disables replace objects and distinguishes unavailable bytes from mismatch. I executed the exact script retargeted only to independent synthetic commit IDs/position2 in my own new bare repository: valid chain0/pass, replace-ref plus graft0/pass with original chain, changed predecessor1/mismatch, missing predecessor2/incomplete. No original Gitseq graph accessed or its558commit run independently claimed. The former cat-file-only false acceptance is gone.\n\nLevel2 anchors are now caller-supplied prior level2 proofs, same sequence/exact predecessor position/digest, with held-but-unproved bytes and shallow ends excluded. The chain claim is expressly conditional on a trusted anchor's correctness; report lists that trust and level3 excludes prior authorship. dap1's signed-intent locations/domain/payload/key/signature encodings and unsigned-input behavior are specified and agree with existing bytes/sign.ts. Git profiles are expressly absent, so level3 stops incomplete/profile. Per-case vectors now specify event, predecessor source, anchors, requested level, depth and full expected report. Owner decision defers actual vectors to first implementation: the note consistently marks them unpublished and forbids conformance claims before publication. This is design approval, not a vector/conformance certification.\n\nTyped report defines null/reached/anchor/trusts, requested level, eleven outcomes/reasons and examples. HTTP specifies event identity/position/digest consistency, UTF8 versus padded RFC4648base64, count1–1000, nonempty contiguous pages/next, empty400/403/404, service ids/SeqHttp/SeqGit, application/did+json and citation dereference to decoded bytes. Reviewed against [DID Core1.0](https://www.w3.org/TR/2022/REC-did-core-20220719/), [RFC4648](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4648), [RFC8032](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8032), [RFC8785](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8785) and official Git raw-object documentation. Shortened genesis document example is explicitly illustrative, not a hash-verifying vector.\n\nArchitecture: sequence identity/citation/host address and byte-chain-authorship/replay boundaries are clear, with a computable adoption plan. Security: no field self-assertion becomes membership, no cache becomes an anchor implicitly, no host locator supplies authority, and fork/head/time/read-access limits remain explicit. The new null reference is scoped to genesis context; retained wire bytes and resolved references have distinct roles. Simplification: exact small